!***************************************************************
! This test is designed to check if CO, OH, H2O, and HCN cooling
! (Neufeld & Kaufman tables) produce reasonable temperature
! evolutions, with cosmic-ray heating, in a gas of 1e6 cm-3 starting
! at 300 K. WARNING: do not use the network for production.
!***************************************************************

KROME-X notes:
- Tgas is evolved (legacy default): the driver sets o.evolve_T = true.
- legacy krome_set_user_crate is the network parameter crate
  (p.crate = 1.3e-17 s^-1).
- data.out now starts with a names header (#time Tgas <species>) and
  the species are in KROME-X (alphabetical) order; plot.py picks them by
  name.
- KROME-X (rtol 1e-8) and legacy (rtol 1e-4) agree to < 0.7 % on every
  column over the whole run; final Tgas 12.886 K in both.
